# What a professional event Wi‑Fi service should include

**QUICK SUMMARY**  
Event Wi‑Fi is not “APs on the day.” A serious scope covers survey of capacity and uses, segmented networks, testing before doors open, support during the show, and a basic failure plan for the main uplink.

## Minimum scope

| Included in a serious service | Often missing in cheap quotes |
| --- | --- |
| Attendance / use cases (guests, POS, production, streaming) | Fixed price with no capacity questions |
| Network segmentation | One flat SSID for everything |
| Tests before open | Install same day, no test |
| Support during the event | Call back the next day only |
| Contingency idea (backup uplink, what to prioritise) | “We’ll see if it fails” |

## Why it matters

At an event, a failure hits queues, payments, or live production. Design and support matter as much as radio coverage.

